result_text:
The change doesn't compile, for two reasons:

1. **Header and definitions don't match.** `DrawViewPart.h` still declares the three functions as `static` and taking two arguments (`owner`, `element`). The new definitions in `DrawViewPart.cpp` are ordinary one-argument member functions, so the compiler finds no declaration to match them.
2. **One caller was never updated.** `CosmeticExtension.cpp` (lines 71-78) still calls `DU::isCosmeticVertex`, `DU::isCosmeticEdge` and `DU::isCenterLine`. Those functions were deleted from DrawUtil, so the calls no longer resolve. It is the only caller.

The rest are cleanups plus one existing null dereference. No CLAUDE.md rule applies to these C++ changes.

